ions of mechanical and utility equipment and reports maintenance, safety, or repair concerns to the appropriate personnel. Assists with residence hall and guest housing turnovers in preparation for summer groups and special events, including making beds, distributing linens, and stocking rooms with required supplies. Operates housekeeping equipment and utilizes cleaning chemicals in accordance with established safety procedures. Performs other duties as assigned. REQUIREMENTS: High school diploma or GED. Ability to handle multiple priorities and demonstrate effective time-management skills. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to lift and/or carry up to 30 pounds frequently and up to 50 pounds occasionally, with or without reasonable accommodation. Ability to push/pull housekeeping carts, equipment, and supplies as required. Ability to stand, walk, bend, stoop, kneel, and reach for extended periods. Ability to tolerate exposure to cleaning chemicals and cleaning-related odors. Ability to wear required personal protective equipment (PPE). Strong interpersonal and customer service skills. Basic computer skills. Previous housekeeping, custodial, or janitorial experience preferred.   TO APPLY:  Submit a cover letter, resume and contact information for at least three current professional references.  Saint Mary is an Equal Opportunity Employer.  Questions: email human resources at  hr@stmary.edu",
